# Kiosk Guardian config. Copy to $GUARDIAN_HOME/guardian.conf (mode 600). The REAL file lives outside git
# (~/oc/fleet-access/guardian-kiosk/) because it names hosts and keys (G7). Nothing below is a real value.
#
# THIS FILE IS DATA, NOT SHELL (R12). It is never sourced. Only these lines are read:
#   KEY="value"   KEY='value'   KEY=value   export KEY='value'   # comment   blank lines
# An unknown key, a bad value, a duplicate key or any other shape (a function, an if, a redirect, a variable reference) makes the whole file bad:
# the agent then runs KILLED (shadow, no actions), audits the line number and key name, and keeps publishing health.
# Inside "double quotes" write \$ for a dollar sign; in 'single quotes' everything is literal. Nothing is ever expanded.
# The safety numbers (the 90 s control limit, the clock skew, the payload caps) are not keys: they are fixed in code.
#
# Allowed keys: GUARDIAN_ROOM GUARDIAN_PUBLISH_CMD GUARDIAN_SUBSCRIBE_CMD GUARDIAN_CONTROL_SUB_CMD GUARDIAN_SUDO
#               GUARDIAN_ROOT_HELPER USB_MIC_PATTERN CANARY_VOLUME PRESENCE_FILE GUARDIAN_PIPE_SSH
GUARDIAN_ROOM="<room-slug>"
# Each command runs under `bash -c`. Publish: topic is $1, the line is on stdin.
# Subscribe: $1 is the room; print "<topic><TAB><payload>" per message, forever.
GUARDIAN_PUBLISH_CMD='<command that publishes stdin to topic $1>'
GUARDIAN_SUBSCRIBE_CMD='<command that streams topic<TAB>payload lines>'
# REQUIRED. Control subscription: $1 = room, $2 = topic; print one raw payload line per message, forever. No message for 90 s = killed.
# Empty or missing = the agent is killed (the old flag command is gone).
GUARDIAN_CONTROL_SUB_CMD='<command that streams one control payload line per message>'
# Extra environment for the transport commands (exported).
# export GUARDIAN_PIPE_SSH='<ssh options for the pipe>'
# The kiosk-sudo path: a command that runs its arguments as root (sudoers NOPASSWD for the root helper only).
GUARDIAN_SUDO="sudo -n"
GUARDIAN_ROOT_HELPER="/usr/local/libexec/eta-guardian-root"
USB_MIC_PATTERN="C270"
# PRESENCE_FILE="/absolute/path/of/the/Presence/heartbeat/file"
# Nightly canary tone level for afplay -v (0.0 to 1.0). The system volume is never changed. Real playback needs mode heal; in shadow it only reports would_do.
# CANARY_VOLUME=0.3
